[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Software Design Document
UID: DOC-SDD
VERSION: 0.1.0
DATE: 2026-10-20

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Software units

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD001
TITLE: Human stimulus
STATEMENT: Human and its patient subclasses shall hold the patient stimulus, including age and sensor validity, and shall not evaluate alarms.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD002
TITLE: AlarmLimits unit
STATEMENT: AlarmLimits shall hold one limit profile and accept_limits shall decide whether a set_limits command is inside the allowed range.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD003
TITLE: AlarmEvaluator unit
STATEMENT: AlarmEvaluator shall be a pure function from a patient and a limit profile to a set of alarms, including the inclusive-limit and sensor-fault rules.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD004
TITLE: PatientMonitor unit
STATEMENT: PatientMonitor shall own attach, start, stop, set_limits, vitals, and alarms, and shall keep the last accepted limits when a command is rejected.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS001
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS005
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD005
TITLE: No lower-class segregation
STATEMENT: The pytest harness shall stay separate from the monitor package. No segregation is claimed for a lower software safety class, and every software item in this increment remains at Class C.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS008
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS009

[[/SECTION]]
